# DIAGNOSTICS

The exit status is 0 if every command exited 0, and 123 if any did not.
`xargs` stops at once with 124 when a command exits 255, 125 when one is killed by a signal, 126 when one could not be run, and 127 when it could not be found; for these two the child says `xargs: execvp` <cmd>`:` and the error.
Its own errors exit 1: `unterminated single quote`, `unterminated double quote`, `backslash at EOF`, `insufficient argument space`, a bad number, and the usage message.

# BUGS

The usage message leaves out `-I`.

POSIX runs <cmd> once when there is no input and no `-r`; `xargs` does not.

`-I`'s arguments are kept under 255 bytes: a <replstr> that would make one longer is left as it is, and an <arg> of 255 bytes or more is cut to 254.

The POSIX namespace has no `/dev/tty`, so `-p` cannot ask, and runs each command without asking; this is untested on VectraOS.

Only `xargs -n 1 echo` has been run on VectraOS; the rest is untested here.
